Advertise a friend share secret so the host can be invite-only.

The host-start side already refuses non-owner guests when --owner-only is
passed. For friend sharing the packaged runner omits --owner-only and passes
--secret <value> instead. A non-empty advertised secret marks the listing
invite-only, and the signaling service relays only guests that present the
matching secret from their https://parsec.gg/g/<peer>/<secret>/ link. The
value is never a constant and is empty unless the owner turned sharing on.

diff --git a/crates/daemon/src/service.rs b/crates/daemon/src/service.rs
--- a/crates/daemon/src/service.rs
+++ b/crates/daemon/src/service.rs
@@ -309,7 +309,11 @@ fn advertisement(name: &str, capacity: u32, players: u32) -> ConnUpdate {
         name: name.to_string(),
         desc: String::new(),
         game_id: String::new(),
-        secret: String::new(),
+        // A friend share secret marks the host invite-only; the signaling
+        // service then relays only guests that carry it in their invite link.
+        secret: flag("--secret")
+            .filter(|secret| secret.len() >= 8)
+            .unwrap_or_default(),
         max_players: capacity,
         players,
         is_public: false,
